// petal-ui prelude — module `ui`
//
// The petal-ui interface: the declarations of the natives a petal-ui host
// provides, and the standard interaction primitives written in Petal over the
// Layer-0 input natives and the Layer-2 draw natives. Embedders register it
// as the package `ui`; a script writes `import ui` and calls these bare or
// as `ui.button`, or `import ui: button`.
// Only declarations marked `pub` are visible to importers; everything else
// (and any name starting with `_`) is module-private.
//
// Rects are records: {x, y, w, h}. Colors are records: {r, g, b} (hex
// literals like #3c8cff work). Button 0 is the left mouse button.

// The package's modules, all re-exported here: `import ui` binds every name
// of each, as if this file declared them.
//
//   ui/input    the input, timing and frame natives
//   ui/draw     the draw natives, geometry, record overloads, clipping,
//               gradients, shadows, elevation, canvases, fonts, colour,
//               compositing and the theme
//   ui/hit      layers, interact, targets, measuring, flow layout and
//               retained drawing
//   ui/text     text helpers, text on a path, text ranges and the clipboard
//   ui/layout   RectCut, motion and pixel-budget word wrap
//   ui/interaction focus, list and scroll state, text editing, the popover
//               runtime, drag and drop, the load state and colour text
//   ui/widgets  the drawn widgets, deprecated: bloom owns the widgets, and
//               these are re-exported only until the deprecation period ends
//
// The modules whose names start with `_` are the package's internals:
// `_native` (the private native declarations), `_base`, `_style` and
// `_frame`. Their public names arrive through `ui/draw` and `ui/hit`.
// `ui/drag` is not re-exported: a script that drags writes `import ui/drag`.

pub import ./input
pub import ./draw
pub import ./hit
pub import ./text
pub import ./layout
pub import ./interaction
pub import ./widgets
